SUMMARY:[ATH] Jr. Sewing Machine Basics: Corners (Ages 6-18)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T170000
DTSTAMP:20260815T133111Z
UID:smcl-6a5fe2d64523092f0031a6f3@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to dive into the wonderful world of sewing? Join
  us in the Atherton Makerspace every third Tuesday of the month for Jr. Se
 wing Machine Basics. If you're a curious beginner or just looking for a fu
 n new skill\, Jr. Sewing is the perfect starting point. This class is spe
 cifically designed for kids aged 6-18. We'll teach you the basics\, from t
 hreading a needle to winding a bobbin.\n\nWith hands-on practice\, kids wi
 ll also create a simple sewing project to take home\, leaving with new ski
 lls and something they made themselves.\n\nNo experience is needed. All ma
 terials will be provided. Space is limited\, so be sure to sign up online 
 at smcl.org or ask a staff member to assist you with registration.\n\nAges
 : 6-11\, 12-18\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons
 .com/events/6a5fe2d64523092f0031a6f3\nLast synced: 2026-08-15 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5fe2d64523092f0031a6f3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] End of Summer Drive-In Movie Night: Toy Story 4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T184500
DTSTAMP:20260815T133111Z
UID:smcl-6a513c78f4e5db3d00c0dabe@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Summer may be winding down\, but that doesn’t mean the party
  has to stop yet! Come enjoy a family movie at the library\, where we’ll
  be hosting an afternoon filled with fun and games\, arts and crafts\, and
 \, of course\, a great film to close out the evening. First\, join us earl
 y at 4 PM to play giant-sized games\, build your own cardboard car for our
  special movie night\, and try other fun tie-in crafts. Then\, “drive”
  outside to our Makerspace Deck for the screening to start at 5 PM. All ag
 es are welcome! \n\nWe’ll be watching Toy Story 4: “Woody has always b
 een confident about his place in the world...and that his priority is taki
 ng care of his kid\, whether that’s Andy or Bonnie. But when Bonnie adds
  a reluctant new toy called “Forky” to her room\, a road trip adventur
 e alongside old and new friends will show Woody how big the world can be f
 or a toy.” (1h 40m)\n\nAges: 6-11\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://s
 mcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a513c78f4e5db3d00c0dabe\nLast synced: 2026-0
 8-15 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a513c78f4e5db3d00c0dabe
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Paws for Tales
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T180000
DTSTAMP:20260815T133111Z
UID:smcl-6a5a9d53daaaf4f51a201c01@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a reluctant reader? Sign your child up for a sessi
 on to practice reading with a therapy dog at the library.\n\nStudies show 
 that children who may not want to read in front of their peers are much le
 ss anxious with an animal present. Children don't perceive animals as judg
 mental\, and reading to an animal helps them become more confident readers
 . We’d like to thank our partners for making this possible: Pet Assisted
  Therapy teams and their handlers from the Peninsula Humane Society & the 
 SPCA's Paws for Tales program.\n\nSpace is limited\, so register early for
  your 10-minute slot at smcl.org/pawsfortales! We do our best to accommoda
 te drop-ins whenever possible\, so feel free to stop by!\n\nAges: 6-11\nRe
 gistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9d53da
 aaf4f51a201c01\nLast synced: 2026-08-15 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9d53daaaf4f51a201c01
END:VEVENT
