BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SC] Paper Airplanes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T120000
DTSTAMP:20260815T133111Z
UID:hiller-283780@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Paper Airplanes\n\nEveryone loves paper airplanes. We turn int
 o test pilots just by folding sheets of paper. We make them to see how fas
 t they will go or how far they will fly\, we even try to do aerobatics wit
 h them.\n\nOne of the top paper airplane makers in the country (and world 
 record holder)\, John Collins\, will join us for an expert demonstration o
 f the wonder\, delight and aeronautic capabilities of hand made paper glid
 ers. John is world distance paper airplane record holder and a master pape
 r airplane builder. John has written a number of books on building paper a
 irplanes that will be available at the event and John will make sure he pe
 rsonalizes it just for you.\n\n \n\n \n\nJohn’s discussions and demons
 trations will last approximately 45 minutes. No reservations are required 
 and the event…\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://www.hiller.org/event/p
 aper-airplanes/\nLast synced: 2026-08-15 06:31 PDT
LOCATION:Hiller Aviation Museum\, 601 Skyway Rd.\, San Carlos
URL:https://www.hiller.org/event/paper-airplanes/
END:VEVENT
